  "label": "burning things that don't mean anything to you is mapped onto cremation ovens",
  "description": "The text 'burning things that don't mean anything to you' is metaphorically mapped onto the visual entity 'cremation_ovens'. The cremation ovens, historically associated with mass destruction and genocide, are used as a visual metaphor for the act of burning things deemed irrelevant or worthless. This mapping creates an analogical relationship where the visual material (cremation ovens) represents the textual concept (burning valueless things), despite the profound historical and emotional weight of the visual. The mapping is established through the juxtaposition of the text with the image, where the cremation ovens serve as the visual embodiment of the textual metaphor.",
